From 1a2c8d335a9936efa16a2fcdae9441f53516badd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelinek <jakub@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:13:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i386: Fix up a typo in __enclv_generic macro in sgxintrin.h
 [PR128015]

This macro contains an obvious typo, compared to other __en*_generic
which contain after the asm template:
	   : "=a" (retval), "=b" (b), "=c" (c), "=d" (d)\
	   : "a" (leaf), "b" (b), "c" (c), "d" (d)	\
	   : "cc")
it had:
	   : "=a" (retval), "=b" (b), "=c" (b), "=d" (d)\
	   : "a" (leaf), "b" (b), "c" (c), "d" (d)	\
	   : "cc")
so, the value of bx and cx registers was stored into the same
macro argument (__D[0]) instead of bx stored into __D[0] and
cx stored into __D[1].  I've grepped around and didn't find
similar typos elsewhere in the header and I think this is kind of
hard to test in the testsuite in userland.

Fixed the obvious way.

2026-10-20  Jakub Jelinek  <jakub@redhat.com>

	PR target/128015
	* config/i386/sgxintrin.h (__enclv_generic): Fix a typo.

(cherry picked from commit d5b9d3a458a58766d03445441e3952d43824c402)
---
 gcc/config/i386/sgxintrin.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/i386/sgxintrin.h b/gcc/config/i386/sgxintrin.h
index 671b6deb41fc..62dc461de724 100644
--- a/gcc/config/i386/sgxintrin.h
+++ b/gcc/config/i386/sgxintrin.h
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@
 
 #define __enclv_generic(leaf, b, c, d, retval)		\
   __asm__ __volatile__("enclv\n\t"			\
-	   : "=a" (retval), "=b" (b), "=c" (b), "=d" (d)\
+	   : "=a" (retval), "=b" (b), "=c" (c), "=d" (d)\
 	   : "a" (leaf), "b" (b), "c" (c), "d" (d)	\
 	   : "cc")
 
